 {
  "text": "Hi Ricardo, this is Amy, from the Miami office. A quick message about next week. Monday is a holiday in the United States, so the office is closed. The team meeting is on Tuesday, not on Monday, at ten in the morning. On Wednesday, the director is in New York, so there is no meeting. Your call with São Paulo is on Thursday, in the afternoon. Have a nice weekend!",
  "voice": "ellen",
  "file": "a12_listening1.mp3"
 },
 {
  "text": "Hi, this is Paul, from the fourth floor. A small piece of advice about dates in the United States. Here, we write the month first, and then the day. So five, ten is May tenth. It is not the fifth of October. In Brazil, it is the other way. At a bank, this is very important. Check the date two times, every time. It is a small thing, and it saves a big problem.",
  "voice": "arthur",
  "file": "a12_listening2.mp3"
 },
